{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1697"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/olympics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__olympics.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",908],["+","Not every substance stays on the list for ever. The World Anti-Doping Agency, which took over the prohibited list in 2004, removed caffeine from it with effect from 1 January 2004, although the stimulant demonstrably improves endurance and muscle performance; the IOC had banned it above a urine threshold since 1984, and it has since remained only on WADA's monitoring programme. Clenbuterol, by contrast, is banned in any amount, which is why a mere trace cost Contador two titles.\n\n"],["=",183]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",816],["+","Nicht jede Substanz bleibt für immer auf der Liste. Die Welt-Anti-Doping-Agentur WADA, die die Verbotsliste 2004 übernahm, strich Koffein mit Wirkung zum 1. Januar 2004, obwohl der Wirkstoff Ausdauer und Muskelleistung nachweislich steigert; das IOC hatte ihn seit 1984 oberhalb eines Grenzwerts im Urin verboten, seither steht er nur noch im Überwachungsprogramm der WADA. Clenbuterol ist dagegen in jeder Menge verboten, weshalb schon eine Spur Contador zwei Titel kostete.\n\n"],["=",175]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1697"},"reason":"a1697: bodyEn/De: \"Clenbuterol … is banned in any amount\" → \"had no threshold at all\" (WADA has since added minimum reporting levels for meat contaminants) — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberto_Contador","by":"enrich batch 213","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1553-a2081.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberto_Contador"}]},
